Fix independent front/back GL_COLOR_MATERIAL tracking in gl4es's GLES2
fixed-pipeline emulator.

OpenGL keeps one active GL_COLOR_MATERIAL_FACE. Changing it from GL_FRONT
to GL_BACK means subsequent glColor calls update only the back material;
the previously tracked front material retains its last value. gl4es instead
remembered a mode independently for both faces and generated both lighting
paths from the same per-vertex gl_Color. With two-sided lighting this made
back-face accent colors leak onto front-facing polygons.

Track the active face explicitly, mirror glColor updates into the selected
material state, and make the generated shader substitute gl_Color only for
the selected face. Also expose/preserve GL_COLOR_MATERIAL_FACE and
GL_COLOR_MATERIAL_PARAMETER through glGet and glPushAttrib(GL_LIGHTING_BIT).

The gl-repl logo example is the integration regression: its exterior remains
near-white while its visible interior back faces retain their cyan/magenta
materials in the Emscripten/WebGL build.

Applied by scripts/web-deps.sh after cloning the pinned gl4es checkout.
